{"id":"st429-6","designation":"ST 429-6","title":"D-Cinema Packaging — MXF Track File Essence Encryption","state":"active","suite":"429","official":{"family_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/doc/st429-6/","latest_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/latest/st429-6/","checked_at":"2026-11-18"},"scope":"This standard defines a syntax for encrypted Track Files, i.e. MXF files containing a single Essence Track, and specifies a matching reference decryption model. It uses the AES cipher algorithm for essence encryption and, optionally, the HMAC-SHA1 algorithm for essence integrity. This standard assumes that the cryptographic keys necessary to decrypt and verify the integrity of encrypted Track Files will be available upon demand. More precisely, it does not specify the fashion with which cryptographic keys and usage rights are managed. In addition, this document does not address, but does not preclude, the use of watermarking, fingerprinting or other security techniques to provide additional protection.","outline":[{"level":1,"title":"D-Cinema Packaging — Track File Encryption","page":1},{"level":2,"title":"Table of contents","page":1},{"level":2,"title":"Foreword","page":1},{"level":2,"title":"1Scope","page":1},{"level":2,"title":"2Conformance","page":1},{"level":2,"title":"3Normative references","page":1},{"level":2,"title":"4Terms and definitions","page":1},{"level":2,"title":"5Overview","page":1},{"level":2,"title":"6Encrypted Essence Container","page":1},{"level":2,"title":"7Cryptographic Framework","page":1},{"level":3,"title":"7.1General","page":1},{"level":3,"title":"7.2Cryptographic Framework Key","page":1},{"level":3,"title":"7.3Length","page":1},{"level":3,"title":"7.4Context SR","page":1},{"level":2,"title":"8Cryptographic Context","page":1},{"level":3,"title":"8.1General","page":1},{"level":3,"title":"8.2Cryptographic Context Key","page":1},{"level":3,"title":"8.3Length","page":1},{"level":3,"title":"8.4Context ID","page":1},{"level":3,"title":"8.5Source Essence Container